 "notes": "1-bit photocopy, 5400x4143. Frame on all four sides: thick bar (speckled), white gap, thin inner rule (innermost); the page is turned ~0.4 deg and the sides bow (bottom 3977 -> 4009 across). Outline ~1.5 px inside the thin rule's inner edge, measured on every 2nd px (bars despeckled along the side), robust fit, points <=150 px apart. Corner arcs (thick + thin) in all four corners, circles R 202-217 px (rms <0.45 px); the thin arc joins each side rule through a ~6 px joggle (stub), at TL x ~566 / y ~606, TR x ~4757 / y ~640, BL x ~545 / y ~3762, BR x ~4757 / y ~3790; the outline follows the thin arc's inner edge and steps round each joggle, so stubs stay outside. Kind (b): hatched and solid blocks run into the top rule (x ~600-700, ~3470-3580, ~2100-2230), the right rule (y ~1960-2020, ~2760-2920, ~3260-3420) and the bottom rule (x ~4050-4510); hatched blocks cross the TL arc, and the part beyond the arc is outside. Right side y ~1950-2010: a map line runs 1 px inside the thin rule, the outline sits on it. remove: (1) the rotated CITY & COUNTY ... ZONE MAP title, LEGEND swatches, legend text and the scale bar (top right, no ruled box, between hatched blocks on the left/below and the TR arc and right rule): a 12-point outline ~4-8 px outside the ink; on the right it runs in the 3-8 px gap between the CITY & COUNTY line and the right rule/arc; two ditto marks at the bottom-left of the legend (4394-4401 and 4452-4457, y ~1177-1187) touch a hatch line and are left outside; the hatched street line touching the COMMERCIAL swatch's top-left corner stays map; (2) the SECTION 12 badge (ring centre 4837.8,3906.9, radius 58.6), an octagon 5 px outside, crossing the street lines it sits on. No compass rose on this sheet. 'Join Sec. 7/11/13' print outside the frame.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (test-label agent TA, issue #71), 2026-11-21: from the scan and inputs/frame-labels/README.md only (no model output looked at). Sides: inner edge of the innermost rule measured on every 2nd px along each side from luminance profiles, robust local-linear fit, outline 1.5 px inside the edge (first clean paper row); corner arcs from rays out of a fitted centre (inner edge of the thin arc, smoothed by angle), the region beyond each arc cut away; remove blocks from ink extents / connected components at full resolution. Every flagged vertex and the top-ranked ink stretches checked close up. TEST SET: never train on it."
